      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-save-image-(png)-a1361e2c",
        "name": "Save Image (PNG)",
        "description": "This node converts a generated image tensor into PNG byte format, making it suitable for saving, downloading, or passing to external systems. It expects an image tensor in the format [B, 3, H, W] (batch, RGB channels, height, width) with values in the range [0, 1].\n\nThe node first validates the tensor shape and ensures it contains RGB data. It then selects the first image in the batch, clamps values to a valid range, and converts the tensor into a NumPy array with pixel values scaled to [0, 255]. This array is transformed into a PIL image and encoded into PNG format using an in-memory buffer.\n\nA configurable compression level (0–9) allows balancing file size and encoding speed. The final output is raw PNG byte data, which can be directly written to a file or transmitted as needed.",
