    {
      "id": "i0rtavmpk",
      "node_id": "node-load-model-(sdxl)-0c07685d",
      "version_tag": "v1",
      "title": "Load Model (SDXL)",
      "description": {
        "text": {
          "text": {
            "text": {
              "text": {
                "text": {
                  "text": {
                    "text": {
                      "text": "This node prepares a fully loaded Stable Diffusion XL pipeline and extracts its core components for use in a custom generation workflow. The model is already provided by the wrapper as a StableDiffusionXLPipeline, so no checkpoint loading is required—only configuration, validation, and decomposition.\n\nThe node first ensures the model is placed on the desired device (such as GPU). It then performs important validation checks specific to SDXL, including verifying the VAE scaling factor and confirming that the scheduler uses a supported prediction type (epsilon or v_prediction).\n\nOnce validated, the pipeline is split into its main building blocks: UNet, VAE, two text encoders (CLIP-L and CLIP BigG), and the scheduler. All neural network components are switched to evaluation mode to ensure stable inference behavior.\n\nThe extracted components are returned ready for downstream tasks such as prompt encoding, sampling, and decoding within an SDXL-based generation pipeline.",
                      "lineHeight": 14,
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
                    },
                    "lineHeight": 14,
                    "fontSize": 11,
                    "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
                  },
                  "lineHeight": 14,
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
                },
                "lineHeight": 14,
                "fontSize": 11,
                "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
              },
              "lineHeight": 14,
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
            },
            "lineHeight": 14,
            "fontSize": 11,
            "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
          },
          "lineHeight": 14,
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
        },
        "lineHeight": 14,
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-load-model-(sdxl)-0c07685d",
        "name": "Load Model (SDXL)",
        "description": "This node prepares a fully loaded Stable Diffusion XL pipeline and extracts its core components for use in a custom generation workflow. The model is already provided by the wrapper as a StableDiffusionXLPipeline, so no checkpoint loading is required—only configuration, validation, and decomposition.\n\nThe node first ensures the model is placed on the desired device (such as GPU). It then performs important validation checks specific to SDXL, including verifying the VAE scaling factor and confirming that the scheduler uses a supported prediction type (epsilon or v_prediction).\n\nOnce validated, the pipeline is split into its main building blocks: UNet, VAE, two text encoders (CLIP-L and CLIP BigG), and the scheduler. All neural network components are switched to evaluation mode to ensure stable inference behavior.\n\nThe extracted components are returned ready for downstream tasks such as prompt encoding, sampling, and decoding within an SDXL-based generation pipeline.",
        "category": "image_sdxl",
        "owner_id": "112361794260852586879",
        "visibility": "public",
        "organization_id": 1,
