      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-k-sampler-(sdxl)-bd3752dd",
        "name": "K-Sampler (SDXL)",
        "description": "This node implements the core denoising process for Stable Diffusion XL, generating latent images from random noise using classifier-free guidance (CFG). It uses a UNet model along with dual text conditioning (prompt embeddings and pooled embeddings) to iteratively refine noise into a structured latent representation.\nThe node begins by preparing the UNet for inference and setting a deterministic random seed for reproducibility. It initializes latent noise based on the desired output resolution and scales it according to the scheduler’s noise distribution. The scheduler is configured with the specified number of denoising steps, controlling how many refinement iterations will be performed.\nA key part of SDXL is its additional conditioning, which includes both token-level embeddings and pooled embeddings, along with spatial metadata (time_ids) that describe the image size and crop. These are combined for both positive and negative prompts to enable classifier-free guidance.\nDuring the denoising loop, the latents are duplicated and passed through the UNet with both conditional and unconditional inputs. The model predicts noise for each, and CFG is applied to guide the output toward the prompt using the cfg scale. The scheduler then updates the latents at each timestep, progressively transforming noise into meaningful structure.\nThe final output is a latent tensor (sdxl::latent_image) with shape [1, 4, H/8, W/8], which can be passed to a VAE decoder to produce the final image.",
        "category": "image_sdxl",
        "owner_id": "112361794260852586879",
        "visibility": "public",
        "organization_id": 1,
        "edge_node": false,
        "live_version": "v1",
        "created_at": "2026-04-15 09:32:39.867836"
      },
