    {
      "id": "airqa63au",
      "node_id": "node-google-docs-writter--4acac1b5",
      "version_tag": "v1",
      "title": "Google Docs Writer",
      "description": {
        "text": "This node creates or updates a Google Docs document from generated content and optionally embeds a PNG image at a predefined placeholder. It handles the complete Google Docs and Google Drive workflow automatically, allowing AI-generated reports, assignments, posters, or other documents to be exported directly into Google Docs with proper formatting.\n\nIf an image is provided, the node first uploads it to Google Drive using the supplied OAuth access token. The uploaded image is then made publicly readable so it can be inserted into a Google Docs document as an inline image. The node accepts the image either as raw PNG bytes, a file path, or a file-like object, making it compatible with multiple upstream image-producing nodes.\n\nThe node can either create a new Google document using the specified document title or update an existing document when a document ID is supplied. When Append Mode is enabled, new content is inserted at the end of the existing document while preserving all previous content. Otherwise, the new content is inserted from the beginning of the document.\n\nAfter inserting the text, the node automatically applies basic document formatting by converting recognized title and section markers into Google Docs heading styles. Lines beginning with markers such as POSTER TITLE: or ASSIGNMENT TITLE: are formatted as Heading 1, while section headers such as SECTION, INTRODUCTION, CONCLUSION, and [SECTION] are formatted as Heading 2. This allows structured AI-generated content to appear as a properly organized document without requiring manual editing.\n\nIf the document contains the special placeholder [IMAGE_INSERT_HERE], the node locates its exact position, removes the placeholder text, and replaces it with the uploaded image. The image is inserted inline at the marker location using a predefined display size, ensuring that generated diagrams, posters, charts, or illustrations appear in the intended position within the document.\n\nOnce processing is complete, the node returns both the Google Document ID and the document URL, allowing downstream nodes or users to access, share, or continue editing the generated document directly in Google Docs.",
        "lineHeight": 14,
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-google-docs-writter--4acac1b5",
        "name": "Google Docs Writer",
        "description": "This node creates or updates a Google Docs document from generated content and optionally embeds a PNG image at a predefined placeholder. It handles the complete Google Docs and Google Drive workflow automatically, allowing AI-generated reports, assignments, posters, or other documents to be exported directly into Google Docs with proper formatting.\n\nIf an image is provided, the node first uploads it to Google Drive using the supplied OAuth access token. The uploaded image is then made publicly readable so it can be inserted into a Google Docs document as an inline image. The node accepts the image either as raw PNG bytes, a file path, or a file-like object, making it compatible with multiple upstream image-producing nodes.\n\nThe node can either create a new Google document using the specified document title or update an existing document when a document ID is supplied. When Append Mode is enabled, new content is inserted at the end of the existing document while preserving all previous content. Otherwise, the new content is inserted from the beginning of the document.\n\nAfter inserting the text, the node automatically applies basic document formatting by converting recognized title and section markers into Google Docs heading styles. Lines beginning with markers such as POSTER TITLE: or ASSIGNMENT TITLE: are formatted as Heading 1, while section headers such as SECTION, INTRODUCTION, CONCLUSION, and [SECTION] are formatted as Heading 2. This allows structured AI-generated content to appear as a properly organized document without requiring manual editing.\n\nIf the document contains the special placeholder [IMAGE_INSERT_HERE], the node locates its exact position, removes the placeholder text, and replaces it with the uploaded image. The image is inserted inline at the marker location using a predefined display size, ensuring that generated diagrams, posters, charts, or illustrations appear in the intended position within the document.\n\nOnce processing is complete, the node returns both the Google Document ID and the document URL, allowing downstream nodes or users to access, share, or continue editing the generated document directly in Google Docs.",
        "category": "integration",
        "owner_id": "112361794260852586879",
        "visibility": "public",
        "organization_id": 1,
        "edge_node": false,
        "live_version": "v1",
        "created_at": "2026-07-17 17:38:15.012236"
      },
